# The torus bifurcation of cyc_ns with an amplitude dependent frequency of z,
# z' = (beta + i (Om + kap |w|^2)) z - |z|^2 z with kap = 0.8. The return time depends on
# |w|^2 now, which makes alpha1 nonzero. The coefficient does not change, d = -2 gam / T. Own
# test model.
par beta=0.2
Om=2
lam=beta-0.25
r2=x2^2+y2^2
fr=Om+0.8*r2
x1'=beta*x1-fr*y1-(x1^2+y1^2)*x1
y1'=beta*y1+fr*x1-(x1^2+y1^2)*y1
x2'=lam*x2-0.8*y2-r2*(x2-0.5*y2)
y2'=lam*y2+0.8*x2-r2*(y2+0.5*x2)
init x1=0.45,y1=0,x2=0,y2=0
done
